(6. INTEGRAL ABSOLUTE AND RELATIVE FORMAL IMMERSIONS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The q-expansion computations use the dual-level model with a specified) Tj T*
(embedding of mu_p, whose Tate q-expansion cusp is rational. Sending) Tj T*
(\(E,P\) to E/<P> with the canonically identified dual kernel gives a) Tj T*
(Q-isomorphism from the point-level model to this model. This is the) Tj T*
(Fricke transport; it inverts diamonds and sends the point-level A_q) Tj T*
(factor to T_q-D_q-q up to an invertible diamond. Thus the usual) Tj T*
(q-expansion pairing with T_j is at a rational cusp in our conventions.) Tj T*
(The quotients whose cotangent lattices are used have odd orders 3,5,or7.) Tj T*
(Their tame quotients) Tj T*
(of the good modular model at 2 are smooth, and averaging gives the) Tj T*
(saturated invariant differential lattice. The H8 pullback family at 113) Tj T*
(is formed on the formal neighborhoods of a free ordinary orbit. Its) Tj T*
(local quotient is etale even at 2, so the family is smooth of dimension 1.) Tj T*
(No global even-order quotient cotangent assertion is required.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Pure cusp tests use the integral Hecke order, not an equality of Betti) Tj T*
(and Hodge lattices. For a prime-level weight2 space, q-expansion duality) Tj T*
(identifies the actual Z_2 cotangent lattice with Hom_Z2\(T,Z_2\).) Tj T*
(If t lies in 2T, its action on any integral T-stable lattice lies in) Tj T*
(2End\(L\). Consequently operator independence modulo 2 on such a lattice) Tj T*
(implies the required independence in T/2T. This is the only direction) Tj T*
(used. Injective compression is verified by reconstructing every raw) Tj T*
